1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E22 -= Extra.Lap =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,800
麦姬，鲍勃叔叔怎么睡在我的办公室里？
Maggie, what's Uncle Bob doing sleeping in my office?

3
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,620
昨晚他和麦克打扑克
He and Mike played poker last night.

4
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:12,060
-麦克把房间赢回来了 -真的？
- Mike won his room back. - Really?

5
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,960
麦克总算占了点上风，我太高兴了
I'm glad to see Mike getting the upper hand for a change.

6
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:18,780
我也很高兴，不过他把你的车输了
Me, too. Too bad he lost your car.

7
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:23,020
说不定鲍勃叔叔能让我们 搭便车去商店呢
Maybe Uncle Bob wouldn't mind giving us a lift to the store later.

8
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,240
鲍勃叔叔呢？
Where's Uncle Bob?

9
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,800
-还在睡觉吧 -还没醒？
- Still asleep, I guess. - You mean, he's not up yet?

10
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:34,260
谢天谢地，爸，能借你的刮胡膏吗？
Thank you, God. Dad, can I borrow some of your shaving cream?

11
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,500
还要一段时间呢
I'd give it a while.

12
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:40,440
今天真是千载难逢
Come on, Mom. I may never get another chance like this again.

13
00:01:40,628 --> 00:01:42,725
他一连4天早上都给我喷这个
He's sprayed me four mornings in a row.

14
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,400
一连4天早上？
Four mornings in a row?

15
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:51,860
-不留活口 -是，长官
- Take no prisoners. - Yes, sir.

16
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:58,620
-你真坏 -要拥护自己人嘛
- You're bad. - Always support the home team.

17
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:03,284
我和本赌10块钱，鲍勃会打败麦克
Ben and I have $10 saying Uncle Bob beats Mike in the limbo contest.

18
00:02:03,284 --> 00:02:04,584
你们赌吗？
Want a piece of the action?

19
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,620
你们不难为情吗？
You two ought to be ashamed of yourselves...

20
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:07,800
打赌自己哥哥会输
betting against your own brother.

21
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,160
妈妈说得对
Your mother's right, kids.

22
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:13,240
这是麦克的主意，赢了他给钱
But it was Mike's idea. I mean, he said he'd cover any bet against him.

23
00:02:13,261 --> 00:02:17,702
-而且是1赔3 -1赔3，哇
- And he's giving 3-to-1 odds. - 3-to1, whoa.

24
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,660
-杰森 -只是痒痒了
- Jason. - I'm just scratching.

25
00:02:26,007 --> 00:02:27,068
麦克？
Mike?

26
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,160
他死了
He's dead.

27
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:33,900
我的天
Oh, my God.

28
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,660
我只想说在丧礼上哭泣.
For those of you that cried at the funeral...

29
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,400
并不是丢脸的事
I just want to say that it's nothing to be ashamed of.

30
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,600
谢谢，麦姬
Thank you, Maggie.

31
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:05,160
准备好了吗？
Well, are we all ready?

32
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:10,920
-感觉很不舒服 -开始后就会习来惯了
- This feels kind of strange, Mom. - It won't after we get started, honey.

33
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,720
这是鲍勃叔叔的纪念仪式
Uncle Bob called this a remembering session.

34
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,400
每当有家人去世.
When someone in my family passed on...

35
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,520
鲍勃叔叔就会引领我们去追思
Uncle Bob would lead us all in sharing fond memories of that person.

36
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,580
而且称之为“亲爱的死家伙”
Whom he would lovingly refer to as "The dearly defunct."

37
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:25,920
谁要开始？
Who wants to start?

38
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,140
好吧，我来
Okay, then, I will.

39
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,500
我小时候.
When I was a little girl...

40
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,200
想成为舞蹈家
I wanted to be a dancer.

41
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,400
知道为什么吗？
And do you know why?

42
00:03:39,981 --> 00:03:41,077
为什么？
Why?

43
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:43,980
因为鲍勃叔叔带我去看了第一场芭蕾
Because Uncle Bob took me to my very first ballet.

44
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:47,740
记得他说过“她们用脚尖走路..”
And I remember he said, "They walk around on their toes...

45
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:52,660
“而且挥舞臂膀，这些动作很不合理”
"they do flapping things with their arms, and it doesn't make any sense.

46
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:56,600
“但是很美，对吗？”
"But it's pretty, ain't it?"

47
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,980
记得我割掉盲肠后.
Remember when I had my appendix taken out...

48
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:03,880
鲍勃叔叔用瓶子装了起来
and Uncle Bob brought me one in a jar and told me not to worry...

49
00:04:03,971 --> 00:04:05,977
他说知道怎么放回去
'cause he knew how to put it back in.

50
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:09,280
护士过来了，他就拿出瓶子.
Yeah, and when the nurse came, he showed her the jar...

51
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,960
说是汽水贩卖机上出来的
and said he got it out of the soda machine.

52
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:13,260
而且他要退款
And then he said he wanted his quarter back.

53
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,300
还记得他超车时的动作吗？
And remember what to do when passing slow cars on the road?

54
00:04:18,586 --> 00:04:20,319
划.
Stroke.

55
00:04:20,721 --> 00:04:22,283
划.
Stroke.

56
00:04:22,523 --> 00:04:24,085
划.
Stroke.

57
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:27,640
我记得最有趣的是.
I remember how much fun it was...

58
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,920
鲍勃叔叔总让麦克出糗
when Uncle Bob would make Mike lose.

59
00:04:32,066 --> 00:04:33,127
什么？
What?

60
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:38,180
他跑得比你快，投篮比你准 扑克总是赢你
He could run faster, shoot baskets better. He played games like a champ.

61
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,480
-是我让他的 -是吗？
- I let him win. - Sure you did.

62
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,540
记得上次他来吗？
Remember the last visit?

63
00:04:43,878 --> 00:04:47,477
最后冲刺，两人相差甚远
They're in the homestretch and it's not even close.

64
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:52,140
杰森，他又输了，他肯定伤心死了
Jason, he lost again. He'll be crushed.

65
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,280
我知道，他尽了全力
I know. He tries so hard, too.

66
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,660
他来了
Here he comes.

67
00:04:58,259 --> 00:05:01,300
-谁跑第一了？ -鲍勃叔叔遥遥领先
- And the winner is? - Uncle Bob by a mile.

68
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,820
鲍勃叔叔!
Uncle Bob! Uncle Bob!

69
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,900
鲍勃叔叔!
B-O-B. Uncle Bob!

70
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:10,240
好了，好了，纸币扔过来
Please, please. Just throw paper money.

71
00:05:12,039 --> 00:05:13,942
恭喜你
Congratulations.

72
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,580
今天耍够了我儿子没有？
Are you through humiliating my son for the evening?

73
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:19,580
-不好说，凯罗？ -还来得及
- I don't know. Carol? - We can make it if we hurry.

74
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,060
来吧
Let's do it.

75
00:05:32,526 --> 00:05:34,293
于是另一个人说.
So the other fellow says:

76
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:36,380
“如果我能那样走路，就不需要爽身粉了”
"If I could walk that way, I wouldn't need talcum powder."

77
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,380
还好你不是那个擦爽身粉的人
At least you're not the kind of guy who likes to rub it in.

78
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:41,500
谢谢你们合作
Thanks for the help, guys.

79
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,540
开玩笑，我们就喜欢这样
Are you kidding? We live for stuff like this.

80
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,540
-儿子，别让他们取笑 -我还受得了
- Don't let them tease you, Son. - That's all right, Dad. I can take it.

81
00:05:49,543 --> 00:05:52,243
好样的，要比萨饼吗？
Attaboy. You want some pizza?

82
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,360
鲍勃叔叔中途买了一份
Uncle Bob stopped for one on the way back.

83
00:05:56,460 --> 00:06:00,780
算了，别气馁，我最喜欢的外甥是你
Come on, pal. Don't take it so hard. You know you're my favorite nephew.

84
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:04,600
-你叫什么来着？ -这次让你赢了
- What's your name again? - All right, look, you beat me again...

85
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:07,080
但我还年轻，迟早会胜过你
but I'm young, and sooner or later I'm going to come out on top.

86
00:06:07,161 --> 00:06:11,431
他还想受罪，明早再比
Glutton for punishment. Shall we say running shoes at dawn?

87
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,400
-好的 -好吧
- You're on. - All right.

88
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,040
看谁先到浴室
I'm first in the shower.

89
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,480
这回怎样？
How about that.

90
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,500
麦克总算赢你了
Mike finally got the best of you at something.

91
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:22,860
不见得，水龙头被我拿走了
Not really. I took the knobs off the shower.

92
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,840
我当时不是要淋浴
I didn't want to take a shower.

93
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,760
麦克，你能回忆起什么？
Your turn, Mike. What do you remember?

94
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:34,400
2，J，K，一对7
Deuces, jacks, man with an ax. Pair of natural sevens takes all.

95
00:06:36,157 --> 00:06:37,423
扑克？
That's poker.

96
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:41,540
我喜欢跟鲍勃叔叔打扑克 尽管老是输
I loved to play poker with Uncle Bob, even if he did always win.

97
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:52,220
她是一位美丽的姑娘
Boy, she was some beautiful dame.

98
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:58,260
还以为能天长地久 战争爆发了，她就逃了
I thought we'd always be together. Then the war came. She shipped out.

99
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,880
我送了她一条香烟，到你了
I gave her a carton of cigarettes. Your bet.

100
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:07,320
如斯悲壮，你的爱情人生
Yeah, that's some sad story. I mean, the love of your life.

101
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:12,460
-后来又遇到谁了？ -都比不上她，一对J
- Didn't you ever meet anyone else? - No one like her. Two jacks.

102
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,880
爱是永不枯竭的
We'll always have Milwaukee.

103
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,100
鲍勃叔叔.
Hey, Uncle Bob...

104
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:24,340
我心仪几何课上的一位女同学
there's this girl in my geometry class that I like.

105
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:28,200
-每次看到她，我都会打颤 -就多穿点
- When I look at her, I get the chills. - Put a jacket on.

106
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,560
你几何才60多分，同志仍需努力
You got a D in geometry. Now, you can do better than that, you hear?

107
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:34,840
-我正在努力了
-1 - I know. I'm trying. - One.

108
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:39,000
-再努力点 -我会的
- Try harder. - I will.

109
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:40,120
我押10块
I bet $10.

110
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:46,100
我接受，加注10块
All right, I'll see your $10, and I'll raise $10 more.

111
00:07:46,927 --> 00:07:50,435
-好，什么牌？ -三条1
- Call. What have you got? - I got three aces.

112
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,760
满堂红，三条9，一对4
Full house, nines and fours.

113
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,880
怎么老是你赢
I can't believe it, you win every hand.

114
00:07:56,740 --> 00:08:00,320
小麦克，我年纪是你的4倍，我有经验
Mikey, Mikey, I'm four times older than you. I've got experience.

115
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:03,800
你也会有经验的，但我不会让你追上
One day you'll have experience, though I wouldn't hold my breath.

116
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:07,160
天哪!看看时间
Holy mackerel! Would you look at the time?

117
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,800
玩得这么晚，你妈妈会宰了我
Your mother's going to kill me for keeping you up this late.

118
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,300
没关系
Oh, no, that's okay. Really.

119
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,760
兴你有关的事，她都会从宽处理
She lets me get away with everything when it comes to you.

120
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:17,520
是吗？那么我们到城里弄个刺青
She does? Let's go downtown and get some tattoos.

121
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,400
-刺青？ -开玩笑的
- You got tattooed? - He was just kidding.

122
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,700
我从鲍勃叔叔身上学到最重要的是.
The most important thing I ever learned from Uncle Bob...

123
00:08:27,001 --> 00:08:29,234
做人要口是心非
was just never draw to an inside straight.

124
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,420
记得那次感来恩节.
Hey, you remember that Thanksgiving...

125
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:33,880
鲍勃叔叔把整只火鸡.
when Uncle Bob brought the whole turkey out...

126
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:35,900
推到多丽思老姑妈面前
and he put it in front of big, old Aunt Doris?

127
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:40,300
他说“你先吃，我们的火鸡马上就来了”
And he said, "You go ahead and start. Ours will be out in a minute."

128
00:08:45,786 --> 00:08:49,419
凌晨3点半把我弄醒
All right, already. Look, you wake me up at 3:30 in the morning.

129
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,660
我也算了
I say, "No problem."

130
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:53,160
我下去给你弄点吃的吧
I come down here and what do I get for you?

131
00:08:54,728 --> 00:08:56,028
全脂牛奶
Buttermilk.

132
00:08:56,096 --> 00:08:58,261
我最讨厌全脂牛奶了
That's right, buttermilk. I hate buttermilk.

133
00:08:58,265 --> 00:09:01,033
不过我这下要喝了
But I'm going to drink some right now. You know why?

134
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:03,080
因为你喜欢
Because you like it. That's right.

135
00:09:09,243 --> 00:09:10,748
够朋友了吧？
There, am I your buddy or what?

136
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,760
当然了
You betcha.

137
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,660
早上好
Morning, Mike.

138
00:09:38,138 --> 00:09:42,169
做梦而已，不是真的
It was just a dream. It didn't really happen.

139
00:09:43,978 --> 00:09:47,918
我的床，我爱你 谢谢你把它变成一个梦
My bed, I love you. Thank you for making it only a dream.

140
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,240
还有我的枕头
And my pillow.

141
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,500
我爱你枕头
I love you, pillow.

142
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:58,980
早餐好了
Breakfast is ready.

143
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,960
听我解释
I can explain all this.

144
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,620
不必了
Don't bother, Mike.

145
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:08,980
你和枕头之间的事，我们早就知道了
We've known about you and your pillow for a long time now.

146
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,680
她不会懂的
She just doesn't understand.

147
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,360
对不起，起床晚了
Sorry, I'm late, guys.

148
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:21,880
昨夜做了个怪梦
I just had this really weird nightmare last night.

149
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,380
大考结束前1分钟.
Is that the one where you show up for your final exam...

150
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:25,980
你才进入考场？
with less than a minute to go?

151
00:10:27,121 --> 00:10:28,683
但这是真人真事
No, that actually happened.

152
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:32,940
昨晚的梦是荒唐的 醒过来我还真高兴呢
But it was just as crazy. I mean, I was pretty glad when I woke up.

153
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:34,040
我同意
I'll say.

154
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,760
现在大家都来了.
Well, now that we're all here...

155
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,140
是谁昨晚把牛奶撒了一地？
does anyone want to tell me who spilled buttermilk on the floor?

156
00:10:43,804 --> 00:10:45,673
你招认就是了
A simple confession will do.

157
00:10:46,774 --> 00:10:50,043
-没事吧？ -没事
- Are you all right, Mike? - Yeah.

158
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,420
-怎么了？ -没什么
- What happened? - Nothing.

159
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:54,680
有块东西跑错了管道
Something just went down the wrong pipe.

160
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:00,140
这下麻烦了
I'm in big trouble.

161
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,740
猜字游戏迷们，赛事愈发激烈了
And the tension's really building here, charade fans.

162
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,220
女士们领先，但麦克.西弗要追上了
The girls are ahead, and Mike Seaver's coming up for his next turn.

163
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:12,640
麦克，都半夜了 今晚就到此为止吧？
It's almost midnight, Mike. Can't we just call it a night?

164
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,480
正玩得开心呢
What, and end all the fun?

165
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,480
-我累了 -我也是
- I'm tired. - Me, too.

166
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,620
别这样，好，再来猜
Come on. Okay, here we go, Dad.

167
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:26,800
电影名，三个字，第一个字
It's a movie. Three words. First word.

168
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,700
怪.
Sounds like a monster.

169
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:33,360
开车怪
A monster with a car.

170
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:36,600
又是<哥斯拉>？
Oh, no, not another Godzilla movie.

171
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:40,560
<哥斯拉>的第二个字是？
Ben, what's the second word in every Godzilla movie?

172
00:11:40,761 --> 00:11:43,461
-斯 -对
- Meets. - Right.

173
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:47,200
哥斯拉大战玛格丽特
Godzilla meets... Margaret Thatcher.

174
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:52,706
我提示一个，<科学怪人> 我睡了
I'll give you a hint. It's Frankenstein. I'm going to bed.

175
00:11:52,706 --> 00:11:53,940
-我也睡了 -谢天谢地
- Me, too. Let's go up. - Thank God.

176
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:58,460
等等，等等
Hey, wait a minute. Wait a minute.

177
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:01,200
玩大富翁吗？
How about a game of Monopoly?

178
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:03,840
这种游戏老少皆宜
Now, there's a game that's just fun for all ages.

179
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:05,860
麦克，刚玩过了
Mike, we've played Monopoly.

180
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:11,140
拼字游戏，巴棋戏，跳棋
And we've played Scrabble, Parcheesi, and ball tag.

181
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:16,600
一个晚上不能玩太多的游戏
I mean, there's a limit to how much fun a family can stand in one night.

182
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,100
两小时以前就不行了
And we passed it about two hours ago.

183
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,100
睡觉吧？
Coming, Mike?

184
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,840
我打个电话，看谁还在
No, I think I'll get on the horn and see who's around.

185
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:26,640
半夜三更打电话？
At midnight?

186
00:12:27,775 --> 00:12:30,407
-再玩一把益智游戏好吗？ -好吧
- How about a quick game of Uncle Wiggly? - All right.

187
00:12:30,911 --> 00:12:32,507
答错了
Wrong.

188
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,000
麦克，晚安
Night, Mike.

189
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:45,040
-你没事吧？ -没事，太兴奋罢了
- Mike, you okay? - Yeah, fine, great. Just feeling wonderful.

190
00:12:47,628 --> 00:12:50,032
有什么话要说吗？
Sure you don't want to talk about it for a minute?

191
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,880
没什么，真的
No, there's really nothing to talk about, Dad. Really.

192
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:56,380
好吧，晚安
Okay. Good night.

193
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,740
爸爸，人死后会怎样？
Dad, what happens to people when they die?

194
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,160
这话说起来就长了
This could take longer than a minute.

195
00:13:07,281 --> 00:13:09,412
谈一个晚上也可以
If it takes all night, it's okay by me.

196
00:13:10,784 --> 00:13:11,880
好吧
Okay.

197
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:17,180
有人认为人死后会进天堂地狱
Some people believe that when you die, you go to heaven or hell.

198
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,100
有人认为.
Some people believe that...

199
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,920
人死后会轮回转世
then you come back again to live on earth...

200
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,980
来世的处境.
and the kind of life you have then...

201
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:27,320
要看前世
will depend on the kind of person you were.

202
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:31,600
也有人认为人回轮回.
Some people believe that you keep coming back...

203
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:35,900
来世会不断改善，直到顶点
in a higher form each time until you reach the ultimate.

204
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:37,980
当上职业篮球员？
Professional basketball player?

205
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,240
也许吧
Could be.

206
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,640
若是前世作恶，今世就会当律师
If you're not good, you come back as a lawyer.

207
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:48,620
喜欢恶作剧的人呢？
Where do practical-joking joggers fit in?

208
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:49,940
功德也算高的
Hopefully pretty high.

209
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,840
-爸爸，我见到他了 -谁？
- Dad, I saw him. - You saw who?

210
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:54,780
鲍勃叔叔
Uncle Bob.

211
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,700
昨晚我下来喝牛奶.
Last night I was drinking buttermilk...

212
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:58,700
他走过厨房，活生生的
and he ran through the kitchen, just like he was alive.

213
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:00,080
你是做梦吧
Maybe you were dreaming.

214
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:03,600
-牛奶都撒地上了，记得吗？ -记得
- Dad, the buttermilk spilled, remember? - Yeah.

215
00:14:04,338 --> 00:14:06,878
是不是我疯了？
Was it possible, or am I just losing my mind?

216
00:14:08,509 --> 00:14:11,812
也许是梦游，你的想象力.
You could have been sleepwalking, Mike. You know, the imagination is...

217
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:13,080
我知道你会这么说
I knew you would say that.

218
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,880
你相信有鬼吗？
Dad, do you believe in ghosts?

219
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,180
-我.. -你不信吧
- Well... - I didn't think so.

220
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:22,040
我相信你相信看到鲍勃叔叔了
I believe that you believe that you saw Uncle Bob.

221
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:25,480
真的，他要我干什么？
I did. Dad, what does he want from me?

222
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,360
他说了些什么？
What did he say?

223
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,900
他说“早上好”
He said, "Hi, Mike."

224
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,280
很友好
Sounds pretty friendly.

225
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:36,800
我不知道怎么办，他还会回来的
Dad, I don't know what do. And I know he'll be back.

226
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:43,360
-就跟他聊聊吧 -跟死人聊天？
- Why don't you talk to him? - I should just have a chat with a dead guy?

227
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,880
不然就每晚都玩猜字游戏
Either that or we're going to be playing a lot of charades around here.

228
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,820
不过不能再猜<哥斯拉>了
And you're already out of Godzilla movies.

229
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:52,800
很难说.
I don't know.

230
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:56,460
你怕什么？
What's to be afraid of?

231
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:59,080
他又不是坏人，他可疼你了
You act like he's a bad guy and you know he loved you.

232
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,980
或许他变了
Maybe he's changed.

233
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:05,740
如果你真的相信能再见到鲍勃叔叔.
Mike, if you really believe that you've seen Uncle Bob...

234
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,340
就问问他想要怎样
then you should ask him what he wants.

235
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:12,620
-就像你对待病人一样？ -是的
- You say stuff like this to your patients? - Yes.

236
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,860
这个也要收费？
And they give you money for this?

237
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,160
我信不信鬼不重要
It doesn't matter what I believe, Mike.

238
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:22,160
重要的是你的脑子跟你开了个玩笑
What matters is that even if your mind played a trick on you...

239
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,120
空穴来风，事出有因
it did it for a reason.

240
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,660
寻找答案的最好方法是询问
And the best way of discovering that reason is to ask.

241
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,700
-问鲍勃叔叔 -问你心里面的他
- Uncle Bob. - Or your image of him.

242
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:32,520
懂吗？
You understand?

243
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:44,260
写信问可以吗？
I couldn't just do this by mail?

244
00:15:46,370 --> 00:15:47,780
可以，有地址就行了
Yeah, if you have the address.

245
00:15:55,449 --> 00:15:57,079
好，我来了
Okay. I'm going to do it.

246
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,640
我要走进去，勇者无惧
I'm gonna go in there, I'm gonna face my fear.

247
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,760
男子汉大丈夫，男子汉大丈夫
I'm gonna be a man. I'm gonna be a man.

248
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,840
男子汉大丈夫.
I'm gonna be a man. I'm gonna be a...

249
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,100
明天再做
Starting tomorrow.

250
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:14,920
勇敢，勇敢，勇敢.
Be a man. Be a man. Be a man. Be a man.

251
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,220
到厨房了
I'm in the kitchen.

252
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,520
到冰箱了
I'm at the refrigerator.

253
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,720
牛奶拿出来了
I'm taking out the buttermilk.

254
00:16:42,896 --> 00:16:45,596
只是做梦，不是真的
It was a dream. It didn't really happen.

255
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,340
世上并没有鬼
There's no such thing as ghosts.

256
00:16:50,570 --> 00:16:53,668
我是个男子汉，勇敢面对 鬼魂消失了
I was a man. I faced it and it went away.

257
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,600
再也见不到鲍勃叔叔了
I'll never see Uncle Bob again.

258
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:58,720
早上好
Morning, Mike.

259
00:17:00,414 --> 00:17:01,646
妈妈
Mommy.

260
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:07,560
男子汉!做个男子汉
No, Mike. Be a man. You're gonna be a man.

261
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,020
-鲍勃叔叔？ -还好吧？
- Uncle Bob? - What's up, Mike?

262
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,380
还好，你继续
Nothing. Carry on.

263
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:19,860
记得上次吗？赌10块我会赢你
What about that limbo contest? $10 still says I can beat you, huh?

264
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,202
-你到底想要什么？ -想要什么？
- Look, what do you want from me? - What do I want from you?

265
00:17:22,202 --> 00:17:24,071
想要你的10块钱
I want your $10, right?

266
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,560
我可以给你20，要什么都可以
Look, you can have $20. I don't care. Anything you want.

267
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:28,860
-别缠着我! -缠着你？
- Just quit haunting me! - Haunting you?

268
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:32,260
只是玩玩，别紧张
I was just kidding you, Mike. Try to lighten up.

269
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,380
别碰我
Look, don't touch me.

270
00:17:35,115 --> 00:17:37,519
麦克，别误会
Mike, don't take this wrong...

271
00:17:38,151 --> 00:17:41,600
-你怎么怪怪的？ -我怪怪的？
- but you're acting a little strange. - I'm acting strange?

272
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:44,920
你已经死了，还在厨房跑了10公里？
Look, you're running a 10K in my kitchen and you're dead.

273
00:17:45,625 --> 00:17:46,686
10公里？
10K?

274
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:50,300
-我什么？ -我感到很遗憾，我说你死了
- I'm what? - I'm sorry to have to be the one to tell you.

275
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:53,220
我听到更遗憾
Not half as sorry as I am to hear it.

276
00:17:54,368 --> 00:17:55,839
你肯定我死了？
You're sure about this?

277
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:59,360
对，星期五参加你的葬礼了
Yeah, I'm positive. I went to your funeral on Friday.

278
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,400
葬礼隆重吗？
Good funeral?

279
00:18:04,311 --> 00:18:07,648
很隆重，许多人来了 爸爸哭了
Yeah, good funeral. Lot of people came. Dad cried.

280
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:09,460
杰森这好家伙
Good old Jason, huh?

281
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,920
杰克.霍拉德有没有来？
Did Jack Hollard show up?

282
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,540
他老说自己会先走一步.
He always said he was going to belly-up before...

283
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:21,340
怎么了？我没死!我还活着!
What am I saying? What am I saying? I'm not dead! I'm alive!

284
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,100
差点被你骗了
You had me going for a minute.

285
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,920
他还没听懂我的话
I can see I'm not getting my point across here.

286
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:30,820
鲍勃叔叔 上个星期你都做些什么了？
Look, Uncle Bob, what have you been doing for the last week?

287
00:18:31,671 --> 00:18:34,473
记不清了，像往常一样
I don't know. The usual stuff, I guess.

288
00:18:34,541 --> 00:18:37,582
-例如呢？ -例如跑步.
- Like what? - Like running and...

289
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,020
-有别人说话吗？ -有
- Have you talked to anybody? - Yeah.

290
00:18:42,482 --> 00:18:45,421
-谁？ -当然是你
- Who? - You, of course.

291
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:46,100
还有谁？
Who else?

292
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,820
这就怪了.
You know, that's crazy, but...

293
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:55,780
这个星期只记得跟你说过话
I can't remember talking to anyone else this week but you.

294
00:18:57,400 --> 00:19:00,340
-还记得什么？ -都在跑步
- What do you remember? - Running, mostly.

295
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,640
这星期跑步状态真好
Boy, I had some good runs this week.

296
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,420
鲍勃叔叔，一个星期都在跑步.
Uncle Bob, don't you think it's a little weird...

297
00:19:05,806 --> 00:19:08,438
你不觉得有点怪吗？
to spend a whole week doing nothing but running?

298
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,740
是有点怪
Yeah, that is weird, huh?

299
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,920
很怪
Real weird.

300
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:18,740
为什么我还没意识到呢？
I just don't know why I didn't see it before.

301
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,420
我死了
I'm dead.

302
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:24,800
这样就简单多了
Seems simple enough now, huh?

303
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,380
麦克，谢谢你
I want to thank you, Michael.

304
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,080
不客气
Hey, don't mention it.

305
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,800
这种事情你自个儿知道就好
It was just something I thought you should know.

306
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:36,560
我要走了
I have to go now.

307
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,600
-现在就走？ -是的
- What, right now? - Yeah.

308
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:41,400
-鲍勃叔叔，等等 -我早该走了
- Uncle Bob, wait. - Way past my time.

309
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:44,120
-等等 -什么事？
- Wait, Uncle Bob. - Yes, Michael?

310
00:19:44,511 --> 00:19:47,600
你要去哪？就这么抛开一切？
Where are you going? You just can't leave me here like this.

311
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,980
别担心，麦克，没事的
Don't worry, Michael. It's all right. Really.

312
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:53,420
不，我再也不能见到你了
No, it's not. I mean, I'm never going to see you again!

313
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:56,180
你要走了，留也留不住
You're leaving me, there's not a thing I can do about it, right?

314
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:58,180
-可以留 -什么？
- Sure there is. - What?

315
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,840
留在心里
Remember me.

316
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:06,271
-什么？ -留在心里
- What? - Remember me.

317
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:10,060
还记得你妈妈那次做寿司.
Remember the time your mom made sushi...

318
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:11,900
我们都穿上日本服吗？
and we all dressed up in Japanese costume?

319
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,140
记得，你却打扮成哥斯拉
Yeah, and you came as Godzilla.

320
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,680
我知道这是你最崇拜的明星
I knew it was your favorite movie star.

321
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:22,200
还记得我们讲过的笑话吗？
Remember all the corny jokes we used to tell, huh?

322
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:26,200
-刺猬亲热时怎样？ -战战兢兢
- How do two porcupines make love? - Very carefully.

323
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:31,020
还记得我死后你往我脸上涂剃须膏吗？
Remember the time I died in the den and you put whipped cream on my face?

324
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:35,380
可我不知道你死了
I didn't know you were dead.

325
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,240
等等，如果你死了.
Wait a minute, if you were dead...

326
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,480
你怎么知道剃须膏的事？
how did you know about the whipped cream?

327
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,680
我知道了许多不知道的事
I know a lot of things I didn't know before.

328
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:50,960
麦克，对不起 我总是开你玩笑，让你难看
Mike, I'm sorry I always teased you and tried to embarrass you.

329
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:55,040
没关系，屈辱能锻炼人格
That's okay. I mean, humiliation builds character.

330
00:20:55,182 --> 00:20:56,721
这就对了
There you go then.

331
00:20:58,320 --> 00:21:01,320
我是不会离开你的
You see, I'm not leaving you.

332
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:03,960
我会留在你的心中
I'm in your memory.

333
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:06,920
溶入你的人格里
I'm in your character.

334
00:21:10,130 --> 00:21:11,590
我是你的一部分
I'm part of you.

335
00:21:22,509 --> 00:21:23,570
麦克，再见
Goodbye, Mike.

336
00:21:26,446 --> 00:21:28,042
鲍勃叔叔，再见
Goodbye, Uncle Bob.

337
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:53,740
我还是回去睡觉吧
I guess I'd better get to bed.

338
00:22:01,781 --> 00:22:03,548
除非我其实正在睡觉
Unless I'm already up there.

339
00:22:16,980 --> 00:22:17,880
麦克，早上好
Morning, Mike.

340
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:21,660
-昨晚睡得好吗？ -很好
- Did you sleep all right, last night? - Yeah, no problem.

341
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:24,320
-事情都解决了 -不害怕了？
- I worked the whole thing out. - No more fears?

342
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:26,700
硬汉又怎会害怕
No, not this cowboy.

343
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:29,580
-好，吃早餐吧 -好的
- Great. All right. See you at breakfast. - Okay.

344
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,460
麦克，拜托
Come on, Mike.

345
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:35,100
我说过多少次了，毛巾别到处扔
How many times do I have to tell you not to leave your towels lying around?

346
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:40,400
妈，这毛巾不是我的
